<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grito de Lares</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Lares uprising</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grito de Lares was an uprising against Spanish rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a> on 23 September 1868, planned by Ramón Emeterio Betances from exile. Several hundred rebels took the mountain town of Lares and proclaimed the Republic of Puerto Rico, but Spanish militia defeated them the next day at San Sebastián. The revolt failed, but it became the founding event of Puerto Rican nationalism and is commemorated as a national day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grito-de-lares.jpg" alt="Grito de Lares" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Public Domain Vector: Tektonson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Grito_de_Lares_(current,_medium_blue).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
